  "raw_text": "Step 1: To maximize the slope of the line containing points \\( A \\) and \\( B \\), we should consider the scenario where point \\( A \\) is at the bottom-left corner of its square and point \\( B \\) is at the top-right corner of its square. This will give us the steepest possible line.\n\nStep 2: The coordinates for the bottom-left corner of the first square (with opposite corners at \\((0,0)\\) and \\((2,2)\\)) are \\((0,0)\\).\n\nStep 3: The coordinates for the top-right corner of the second square (with opposite corners at \\((4,2)\\) and \\((5,3)\\)) are \\((5,3)\\).\n\nStep 4: The slope \\( m \\) of the line passing through points \\((0,0)\\) and \\((5,3)\\) can be calculated using the formula for slope between two points \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\):\n\\[ m = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} \\]\nSubstituting the coordinates \\((0,0)\\) and \\((5,3)\\):\n\\[ m = \\frac{3 - 0}{5 - 0} = \\frac{3}{5} \\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{\\frac{3}{5}}<|im_end|>",
